## Claim
Text: "Development Control Department of the Abuja Metropolitan Management Council (AMMC), an agency of the Federal Capital Territory Administration (FCTA)of Nigeria, in 2020 marked 37 Estates for demolition."
Claim date: September 16, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### 1. Does the Abuja Metropolitan Management Council (AMMC) have a department specifically named the "Development Control Department"?
Answer: Yes, the Abuja Metropolitan Management Council (AMMC) has a department named the Development Control Department. As stated in the source, "The Department of Development Control is a multi-disciplinary establishment created in March 2002 out of the then Land, Planning and Survey, Department of FCDA."

Source URL: https://ammcsite.wordpress.com/departments/dodc/

### 2. Is the Abuja Metropolitan Management Council (AMMC) officially recognized as an agency under the Federal Capital Territory Administration (FCTA) of Nigeria?
Answer: Yes, the search result supports this. According to the AMMC's own website, "The Abuja Metropolitan Management Council (AMMC) coordinates six service departments of the Federal Capital Territory Administration to effectively manage and restore the Federal Capital Territory Master Plan," confirming that the AMMC operates under and is part of the Federal Capital Territory Administration (FCTA) structure.

Source URL: https://ammcsite.wordpress.com/

